.TH "APRSFEED" "8" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
aprsfeed \- forward received AX.25 APRS packets to APRS-IS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aprsfeed
.RI "-u callsign [-p passcode] [-I destination] [-h host] [-f logfile] [-v] [-V]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
aprsfeed receives decoded AX.25 packets over RTP, parses eligible APRS
traffic, and forwards it to an APRS-IS server over TCP. It normally receives
packetd output, not receiver audio. The program runs in the foreground and
reconnects after network failures.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-u callsign"
Set APRS-IS login identity. Required.
.TP
.B "\-p passcode"
Set APRS-IS passcode. If omitted, the program derives one from the base
callsign.
.TP
.B "\-I destination"
Set AX.25 input group. Default ax25.mcast.local, port 5004.
.TP
.B "\-h host"
Set APRS-IS server hostname. Default noam.aprs2.net. TCP port is fixed at
14580; -h is not a help option.
.TP
.B "\-f pathname"
Append packet/log output to the file; disables verbose logging to stdout.
.TP
.B "\-v"
Enable logging to standard output when no log file is selected. May be
repeated.
.TP
.B "\-V"
Print version and exit.
.SH NOTES
The program makes an external network connection and forwards received
traffic. Configure the intended callsign and server deliberately. No
command-line option changes the APRS-IS TCP port.
.SH EXAMPLES
Forward a local packet decoder group using the chosen station identity:
.PP
.nf
aprsfeed \-u YOURCALL \-I ax25.local \-h noam.aprs2.net
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
packetd(8), aprs(1), radiod(8)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
